# Verdict Recheck on Returning Launches

Once an install is locked into `RuntimeMode.shell`, the app must NOT
blindly reopen the previously cached URL forever. On every subsequent
launch (`_resumeShell()` branch of `route_pilot.dart`) the app must:

1. Query `marbledescent.com/config.php` again with the same
   attribution POST body.
2. If the backend returns a fresh `ok: true` + `url`, open THAT URL
   in the WebView — even if it differs from the previously cached
   one (partner landing URLs rotate on the backend side).
3. Persist the new URL + expiry (`writeDestination` + `writeExpiry`),
   replacing the old cached values.
4. Only fall back to the cached URL when the fresh request fails or
   there is no network (an expired cached URL is still better than a
   blank screen).

Push URLs keep priority: a one-shot cold-tap link
(`LocalStore.consumeColdPush`) is consumed and opened BEFORE the
normal recheck happens.

Rationale: partner landing rotates over time; a returning user must
always land on the current URL, not a stale one captured at first
launch. Keep the recheck cheap (short attribution wait — 10 s) so
total load stays under the 10 s budget.
